//
// Queue item 26: the static legality predicate, and the SIZE OF THE MAPPING
// SPACE before and after it.
//
// The deliverable of item 26 is a number, not machinery. Doc 38 measured that
// iron's legality prune left a space small enough that its placements are
// hand-authored tables with only seven legal (parallel_heads, parallel_ffn)
// tails; if ours collapses the same way, item 25's instrument plus plain
// enumeration beats any search, and the mapping-work plan reorders. So the two
// space sizes are pinned HERE, exactly, rather than written into a document
// where nothing re-derives them.
//
// No NPU, no XRT, no aircc, no toolchain. study/mapping_space.py reads
// DECLARATIONS -- herd widths, operand routing, scope per seam -- and never a
// routed design, which is the whole claim: the per-column budget that
// ffn_resident_structure.py can only count after a compile is derivable before
// one. pytest is not in the sandbox venv, so this runs as a plain script, the
// convention run_ffn_resident_emulation_tests.lit sets.
//
// THE UNIT CHECKS ARE NOT HERE. study/test_mapping_space.py is collected by
// study/run_host_tests.py's glob and pinned by run_study_host_tests.lit's exact
// count (392). This recipe runs the CENSUS, which is a different arm: the unit
// checks say the predicate is right, this says what it measures. Adding a
// second name for either would be the "doubly covered" mistake queue item 17
// records.
//
// RUN: python3 %S/study/mapping_space.py | FileCheck %s
//
// THE CONTROLS FIRST, AND THEY RUN ON EVERY INVOCATION. A predicate that
// cannot refuse is not a predicate, and one that refuses everything is not one
// either. Both are matched, so a change that breaks either direction goes red
// here rather than shrinking the headline number quietly.
//
// NEGATIVE: queue item 10's own over-budget design -- one herd of [4,1] with
// three herd-direct L3 operands. MEASURED through aircc 2026-08-12: zero
// inbound aie.flow and 12 aie.packet_flow, three streams per column. The
// compiled census reads ZERO surviving circuit ports there and had to be
// widened twice; a static predicate reads the declaration, so it must see the
// three directly.
// CHECK: negative control: one herd [4,1] with 3 herd-direct L3 operands -> 12 of 16 slots, 3 per column, predicted [3, 3, 3, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0] -> REFUSED
//
// POSITIVE: R1's shipped interior, which routes today. The static count must
// reproduce doc 31b section 3.6's MEASURED table with no compiler involved --
// 7 of 16 ports, 4 shim->core + 3 shim->memtile -- and both memtile rows with
// it (the up feed at 4 MM2S / 2 S2MM, the down feed at 4 / 5, which is the
// GeLU fan-out plus the w_down refill).
// CHECK: positive control: R1 interior -> shim MM2S 7/16, 4 shim->core + 3 shim->memtile, 12 cores over 3 herds -> ADMITTED
// CHECK: positive control: R1 memtiles (MM2S, S2MM) [(4, 2), (4, 5)]
//
// The herd inventory, doc 31b section 3.5, MEASURED by sweeping N herds of
// [4,1] in one segment: nine refuse with "'aie.tile' op row index (6) must be
// less than the number of rows in the device (6)", eight place at 100%
// occupancy. Matched in both directions so a core budget that stopped being a
// cliff, or started being one too early, fails here.
// CHECK: herd inventory: 9 herds of [4,1] = 36 tiles -> REFUSED
// CHECK: herd inventory: 8 herds of [4,1] = 32 tiles -> places
// CHECK: herd inventory: 7 herds of [4,1] = 28 tiles -> places
// CHECK: herd inventory: 5 herds of [4,1] = 20 tiles -> places
//
// Doc 23's rule at its sharpest: J7a's three 8-wide herds fetch packed and
// gamma and the budget "is exactly met". Two is legal, three is the packet
// path, and a model that rounded either way would be useless for R2 -- which
// is the increment that walks into this.
// CHECK: J7a control: predicted per-column MM2S [2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2]
//
// THE MEASUREMENT. Both numbers exact. "Before" is after the divisibility the
// builders raise on (Timeloop's first tier, doc 46: "divisors constructed-in,
// capacity rejected") with the raw axis product beside it, because an
// enumerator that generated the raw product would be generating shapes no
// builder will build. Every range behind these is sourced in AXES -- run
// `python3 study/mapping_space.py --axes` to see each bound with the artifact
// that fixes it.
//
// 115,343,360 -> 3,721,772 is a 31x cut, NOT the collapse item 26 anticipated
// from iron's seven hand-authored tails. Doc 48 is the writeup.
// CHECK: space before legality: 115343360 (raw product 293601280)
// CHECK: space after legality: 3721772
//
// The priced subset, and it must be a PROPER subset. Doc 44 as corrected: a
// column over budget is legal-but-degraded, because AIR packet-multiplexes
// rather than refusing, and filtering those points out would hide the exact
// failure mode this study is trying to see. If this line ever read 0 the slope
// would be dead code; if it equalled the line above, the price would not
// discriminate. main() asserts both, so this CHECK is the value, not the shape.
//
// It is 59% of the legal space, which is the single most consequential number
// here: had the per-column budget been made a hard filter -- the proposal doc
// 44 corrects -- 2.18 million routable designs would have been deleted from the
// space, and the silent packet-multiplexing they exhibit would have been
// deleted with them.
// CHECK: of the legal points, 2181680 are priced, not refused
//
// THE SLICES THAT ANSWER "DOES ENUMERATION BEAT SEARCH". Doc 38's SEVEN is a
// two-axis slice of iron's space, not its size, so the honest comparison is
// against the same slice of ours -- the spatial-replication pair. 21 against
// iron's 7: the same order, three times as many. The structural sub-space
// (15,347 shapes) is what a builder and a placement have to exist for, and it
// is three orders above the seven iron hand-authored, which is why copying
// iron's hardcoded-table approach is not open to us.
// CHECK: legal structures: 428, legal (structure, seam vector): 15347
// CHECK: legal (gemm_herd_x, parallel_bands) pairs: 21
// CHECK: legal (gemm_herd_x, norm_herd_x) pairs: 16
//
// The honesty clause, matched so it cannot be dropped: one axis in this space
// is bounded by no artifact in the tree, and the census says which.
// CHECK: axes no artifact bounds: ['parallel_bands']
//
// The verdict last, so a run whose controls printed but whose count went
// vacuous still fails.
// CHECK: PASS
